cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AAA — Accurate Autonomous Adaptation"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Cinqic"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cinqic/AAA"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
abstract: >-
  An experimental research programme investigating whether an artificial system
  can autonomously learn, predict, reason from feedback, adapt, retain useful
  knowledge, detect when that knowledge is inadequate, and improve its future
  behaviour. Its first deliberate specialization is coding, beginning with
  Python: a safe, deterministic environment in which CPython is the external
  ground truth and feedback arrives only after a committed action. Its earlier
  moving-dot benchmarks are retained as evidence and regression benchmarks. The
  emphasis is on protocols capable of disproving the project's own hypotheses.
  No general-intelligence claim is made or supported.
keywords:
  - online learning
  - adaptation
  - program semantics
  - causal evaluation
  - benchmark methodology
  - reproducibility
